  "verbalization": "Cefixime is suggested to have a potential role in treating Streptococcal Infection through a chain of indications that link it to infectious diseases, including Infectious Otitis Media, Gonorrhea, and Respiratory Tract Infectious Disease. These indications are supported by varying levels of confidence, with Cefixime showing the highest confidence in its association with Infectious Otitis Media and Cefprozil, a related antibiotic, in linking to Streptococcal Infection. The indirect pathway through Cefprozil and Cefoxitin, both of which are indicated for Streptococcal Infection, further supports this relationship. The evidence suggests that Cefixime may be repurposed for Streptococcal Infection via its ability to treat related infectious conditions, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Cefixime to be used in the treatment of Streptococcal Infections, particularly in cases where other antibiotics are not effective.",
